      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Presented in the article are the findings of a multicenter prospective clinical trial assessing quality of life of patients with chronic diseases of lower limb veins on the background of administration of nonmicronized diosmin (Vasocet). Specialized questionnaires (CIVIQ-2) appeared to be the most optimal evaluating tools, more precisely catching alterations in patients' quality of life on the background of drug therapy."},
